+      <div class="faq rv d2">
+        <details><summary>Is it really free?</summary><p>Yes. Kokon is open source under the GNU AGPL-3.0 license. No account, no credits, no subscription. It uses your own GPU, so there is nothing to pay for.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>How do I run Qwen-Image 2.1 locally without ComfyUI?</summary><p>Install Kokon and let its setup download the model. Kokon runs Qwen-Image 2.1 through stable-diffusion.cpp, a native engine, so there is no Python, no ComfyUI and no workflow to build. The step-by-step guide is at kokon.app/qwen-image-2-1-local.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Which model does it use?</summary><p>Qwen-Image 2.1 Turbo, the official 8-step version of Qwen&#x27;s image model, which both creates and edits images and leads the open-weights image-editing rankings.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Does it work on AMD or Intel GPUs?</summary><p>Yes, in beta, through the Vulkan engine on Windows with 12 GB of VRAM or more. On NVIDIA it uses CUDA; on Apple Silicon Macs it uses Metal.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>My GPU has 8 GB. Will it work?</summary><p>Not well today. 12 GB is the smallest size that gives good results with this model. On a Mac, 16 GB of unified memory works but slowly; 32 GB is recommended.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Can Claude Code or Cursor generate images with it?</summary><p>Yes. Kokon ships an MCP server: register it once and any MCP client can create, edit, inpaint, expand and upscale images on your GPU, for free and without an API key.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Is it an alternative to Photoshop Generative Fill?</summary><p>For many edits, yes: paint an area and describe what should be there, or remove, replace and add objects. It runs offline and costs nothing, but it is an AI editor, not a full layer-based image editor.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Can I use the images commercially?</summary><p>Not with the default model. The app is open source (AGPL-3.0), but Qwen-Image 2.1 is released under the Qwen Research License: research and evaluation only, no commercial use without a license from the Qwen team. The optional upscaler is also non-commercial (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0).</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Windows says the app is unrecognized. Is it safe?</summary><p>The beta installer is not code-signed yet, so SmartScreen warns about it. Click &quot;More info&quot; and then &quot;Run anyway&quot;. The code is public and every download the app makes is checked against a pinned hash.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>macOS says Kokon cannot be opened. What do I do?</summary><p>The beta is not notarized by Apple yet, so macOS blocks it the first time. Try to open it once, then go to System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security, scroll down and click &quot;Open Anyway&quot;. You only do this once; in-app updates don&#39;t trigger it again.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Does it work offline?</summary><p>Yes. After setup has downloaded the models, everything runs offline.</p></details>
